DescriptionLLM:
ropriations Act, 2016

This bill provides continuing FY2016 appropriations to federal agencies through December 11, 2015, or until the enactment of the applicable appropriations legislation.

It prevents a government shutdown that would otherwise occur when the existing continuing resolution expires on December 11, 2015, because none of the 12 regular appropriations bills for FY2016 have been enacted.

The bill includes provisions that:

- Extend the authority for the Department of Health and Human Services to obligate funds for the Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF) program through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Homeland Security to obligate funds for the National Flood Insurance Program through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Transportation to obligate funds for the Federal Aviation Administration through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Veterans Affairs to obligate funds for certain health care services through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Agriculture to obligate funds for certain nutrition programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of the Interior to obligate funds for certain land and water conservation programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Justice to obligate funds for certain law enforcement programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of State to obligate funds for certain diplomatic and consular programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Defense to obligate funds for certain military operations through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Energy to obligate funds for certain energy programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Education to obligate funds for certain education programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Housing and Urban Development to obligate funds for certain housing programs through December 11, 2015;
- Extend the authority for the Department of Labor to obligate funds for certain employment and training programs through December 11, 2015;
